domitis Pannoniis, per multos annos <NOTE N="268" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1099"></COL> dies 3. 5. 6.</NOTE>  cum finitimis
varia bella gesserunt. Hortante deinde successu,
divisis <NOTE N="269" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1099"></COL> divis  <HI REND="ITALIC">e corr.</HI>  6 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  agminibus, alii Greciam, alii Macedoniam,
omnia prosternentes ferro, petivere, tantusque terror
Gallici nominis erat, ut etiam reges <NOTE N="270" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1099"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  5. reges ipsi B 2.</NOTE>  non lacessiti
pacem ultro <NOTE N="271" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1099"></COL> ultra 6 <SUP>b</SUP> . u. pacem i. precio
1. 1 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  ingenti pecunia mercarentur.
Solus rex Macedoniae Ptolomeus <NOTE N="272" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1099"></COL> pholomeus 3 <SUP>b</SUP> . 6. ptholomeus 2. 5 <SUP>b</SUP> . B 2.</NOTE>  adventum Gallorum
intrepidus audivit, hisque <NOTE N="273" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1099"></COL> hisque  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  isque 2. isque 5. 6.</NOTE>  cum paucis et
 <COL N="1099C"></COL> incompositis, furiis parricidiorum <NOTE N="274" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1099"></COL> parricidorum
1. 1 <SUP>b</SUP> . B 2.</NOTE>  agitatus occurrit.
Igitur Galli duce Belgio ad temptandos Macedonum
 <NOTE N="275" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1099"></COL> a. m. 2.</NOTE>  animos legatos ad Ptolomeum <NOTE N="276" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1099"></COL> ptholomeum 2. 3 <SUP>a</SUP> . 5. B 2. C 1. 3. pholomeum 3 <SUP>b</SUP> . 6.  <HI REND="ITALIC">et ita saepius.</HI></NOTE>  mittunt,
offerentes pacem, si emere velint. Set Ptolomeus
inter suos belli metu pacem <NOTE N="277" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1099"></COL> g. p. 6 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  Gallos petere gloriatus
est, nec minus ferociter se legatis quam inter
inimicos <NOTE N="278" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1099"></COL> inimicos  <HI REND="ITALIC">superscr.</HI>  vel a (micos) C 1.  <HI REND="ITALIC">et ita</HI>  C 3.</NOTE>  jactavit <NOTE N="279" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1099"></COL> se i. 5.</NOTE> , aliter se <NOTE N="280" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1099"></COL> se a. B 2.</NOTE>  pacem datu
rum negando, nisi principes suos <NOTE N="281" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1099"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  5 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  obsides dederint
 <COL N="1100A"></COL> et arma tradiderint; non enim se fidem <NOTE N="282" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1099"></COL> f. se 2. 3. 4? 5. 6.</NOTE>  nisi
inhermibus <NOTE N="283" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1099"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita</HI>  1. 1 <SUP>b</SUP> . inermis 2. 3. 4? 5. 6 <SUP>c</SUP>  B. C. inermibus 6 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  habiturum <NOTE N="284" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1099"></COL> h. fatetur
C.</NOTE> . Renunciata legatione,
risere Galli, undique acclamantes, brevi sensurum,
sibi an illi consulentes <NOTE N="285" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1099"></COL> conludentes 2. colludentes 3 <SUP>a</SUP> . 5. 6.</NOTE>  pacem obtulerint. Interjectis
diebus praelium conseritur; victi Macedones
caeduntur, Ptolomeus multis vulneribus saucius <NOTE N="286" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1099"></COL> sauciatus 1 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE> 
capitur, caput ejus amputatum et lancea <NOTE N="287" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1099"></COL> lancee infixum 2.</NOTE>  fixum
tota acie <NOTE N="288" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1099"></COL> die
6 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  ad terrorem hostium circumfertur. Paucos
ex Macedonibus fuga servavit, ceteri aut capti
aut occisi <NOTE N="289" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1099"></COL> o. sunt B 2.</NOTE> . Tantae <NOTE N="290" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1099"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">c.</HI>  IX.  <HI REND="ITALIC">inc. Leibn.</HI></NOTE>  fecunditatis ea tempestate
Gallorum fuit juventus, ut Asiam omnem velut examine
aliquo <NOTE N="291" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1099"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  B 6. velut aquilo 3 <SUP>b</SUP> . 5. 6. v. aliquo 3 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  inplerent. Denique neque reges
Orientis sine mercennario Gallorum exercitu ulla
bella gesserunt, neque pulsi regno ad alios quam
ad Gallos confugerunt <NOTE N="292" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1099"></COL> tum conf. B4.</NOTE> . Tantus terror Gallici nominis
 <COL N="1100B"></COL> et armorum invicta felicitas erat <NOTE N="293" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1099"></COL> erat f. 2. 3. 4? 5. 6. B. C.</NOTE> , ut aliter
neque magestatem <NOTE N="294" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1099"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita</HI>  1. B2. C1. majestatem  <HI REND="ITALIC">alii.</HI></NOTE>  suam tutam, neque amissam
recuperare se posse sine Gallica virtute arbitrarentur
 <NOTE N="295" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1099"></COL> arbitrabantur
2. 3 <SUP>a</SUP> . B. C.</NOTE> . Itaque in auxilium a rege Bithiniae vocati,
regnum cum eo parta victoria diviserunt, eamque
regionem ex Gallis et Grecis composito nomine Gallo-Greciam
cognominaverunt. Ibi <NOTE N="(193)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="1100" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1100C"></COL> Pergit jam auctoris nostri narratio.</NOTE>  exercitus
Trebirorum pars in patriam <NOTE N="296" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1099"></COL> patria 3 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  remissa, et pars quae
remansit <NOTE N="297" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1099"></COL> remanserat 1. 1 <SUP>b</SUP></NOTE>  Gallicum genus procreavit, et <NOTE N="298" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1099"></COL> quod 2.</NOTE>  duas
linguas deinceps in usu habuit, id est <NOTE N="299" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1099"></COL> i. e.  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  B6.</NOTE>  Gallicam
et Grecam. Denique Galathae <NOTE N="300" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1099"></COL> et g. B6.</NOTE> , qui ex Gallo-Grecis
 <NOTE N="301" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1099"></COL> Gallis
et Grecis 5 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  orti sunt, excepto <NOTE N="(194)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="1100" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1100C"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Excepto—tempore</HI>  ex Hieronymi prooemio
libri II Comment. in Epistolam ad Galatas, Opera
ed. Martianaei IV, p. 255.</NOTE>  sermone Greco, quo
omnis Oriens loquitur, eandem pene proprietatem
sermonis <NOTE N="302" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1099"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  2. 3 <SUP>a</SUP>  5. 6.</NOTE>  habent quam Treberi; nec refert si aliqua
 <COL N="1100C"></COL> exinde corruerint, cum et <NOTE N="303" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1099"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  3 <SUP>b</SUP> . 5. 6 (6 <SUP>c</SUP> ?).</NOTE>  Afri <NOTE N="304" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1099"></COL> affri 3 <SUP>a</SUP> . 5 <SUP>a</SUP> <SUP>b</SUP> . B2. 6.</NOTE>  Fenicum
 <NOTE N="305" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1099"></COL> ph(o)enicem 5 <SUP>b</SUP> .
6 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  linguam nonnulla <NOTE N="306" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1099"></COL> n. ex p. 6.</NOTE>  parte mutaverint, et Latinitas
ipsa et regionibus cottidie mutetur et tempore.</P> <P COM="1100">8 <NOTE N="307" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1099"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">c.</HI>  X.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Leibn.</HI></NOTE> . Igitur Trebirorum dominatus longe lateque
dilatatus usque ad tempora <NOTE N="308" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1099"></COL> r. t. 6 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  Romanorum mansit
inviolatus. Deinde etiam cum Romani totum <NOTE N="309" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1099"></COL> vel  <HI REND="ITALIC">ut videtur superscr.</HI>  C1.  <HI REND="ITALIC">et ita</HI>  C3. 4.</NOTE>  orbem
armis et prudentia <NOTE N="310" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1099"></COL> potentia
6 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  domuissent amicitias <NOTE N="311" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1099"></COL> amicitiam B. C.</NOTE> 
cum Treberibus <NOTE N="312" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1099"></COL> treberis 2. treverensibus B.</NOTE>  et foedus firmissimum iniere, et
 <COL N="1101A"></COL> hanc urbem, propter antiquam nobilitatem et civium
 <NOTE N="313" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1101"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  3 <SUP>b</SUP> . 5. 6.</NOTE>  sibi quodammodo parem dignitatem <NOTE N="314" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1101"></COL> dignitate 1. 1 <SUP>b</SUP> . 3 <SUP>b</SUP>  5. 6 <SUP>c</SUP> . nobilitate vel dignitate 6 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE> ,
secundam Romam <NOTE N="(195)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="1101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1101C"></COL> Ubi primum hoc legatur nomen, nescio;
sed quosdam afferre juvat locos Gestis antiquiores:
Vita S. Deicoli  <CITN>(Acta SS. Jan. I, p. 201)</CITN> :  <HI REND="ITALIC">magnam
Treverim utpote secundam Romam magnos necesse
fuit habere doctores;</HI>  Vita S. Conradi Trev. c. 2 (v.
infra); Vita S. Agritii  <CITN>(Acta SS. Jan. I. p. 773)</CITN> :
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Revolutis enim sanctus pontifex Silvester annalibus
ejusdem civitatis gesta antiquissima continentibus,
ejus excellentiae nobilitatem et antiquissimam dignitatem
sagaciter indagavit, eamque tam propter aedificiorum
firmissimam praeeminentiam quam propter
civium nobiliorum omnibus Galliae ac Germaniae civitatibus
adeo praestare didicit, ut merito nomen secundae
Romae ipsorum judicio Romanorum susceperit;</HI> 
de quo loco cf. praefationem nostram p. 112; ibidem
p. 778;  <HI REND="ITALIC">Igitur sicut Treveris secunda Roma idcirco
vocatur, quia materialis structurae mirabili operositate
illam quondam aemulabatur;</HI>  Historia martyrum
Trever. apud Hontheim Prodr. I, p. 114:  <HI REND="ITALIC">non enim
propter solam aedificiorum aequalitatem, sed etiam
 <COL N="1102C"></COL> propter dignitatum aemulationem haec urbs secunda
Roma est vocata.</HI>  His adde Berengosi librum De inventione
S. Crucis III, c. 1.  <CITN>(Bibl. maxima Patrum
XII, p. 306)</CITN> :  <HI REND="ITALIC">Trevericam urbem famosissimam—quae
tunc temporis eo divitiis et rebus erat opulentior,
quo armis et militibus videbatur esse potentior. Licet
enim fortis esset ex provinciis et civitatibus undique
adjacentibus, divina tamen gratia fortior erat a credentibus;
maxime cum per beatum Eucharium ac
socios ejus ita sterilis esset idololatria et fide fecunda,
quod non immerito Roma vocabatur secunda.</HI>  Friderici
I. vero diploma quod Wyttenbach affert spurium
est. (?)</NOTE>  appellavere. Tunc etiam
Treberi Romana jura et leges habere coeperunt,
quas usque in hodiernum diem <NOTE N="315" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1101"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  5 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  tenere <NOTE N="316" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1101"></COL> habere B.</NOTE>  noscuntur
 <NOTE N="(196)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="1102" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1102C"></COL> Nota hunc locum saec. XII incipiente scriptum.</NOTE> . Hisdem <NOTE N="317" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1101"></COL> Isdem 5. 6. B2. 6.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(197)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="1102" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1102C"></COL> Unde haec auctor sumpserit, equidem cum
aliis nescio.</NOTE>  temporibus venit ad <NOTE N="318" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1101"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  6.</NOTE> 
Treberim <NOTE N="319" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1101"></COL> teberim  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  treberim 1.</NOTE>  Arimaspes <NOTE N="320" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1101"></COL> armaspes
5.</NOTE>  urbis Romae senator et
rector, volens auditam saepius <NOTE N="321" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1101"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  5.</NOTE>  de Treberibus virtutum
eminentiam ipsa suimet melius <NOTE N="322" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1101"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  1. 1 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  experiri
sententia. Cui Treberi idem <NOTE N="323" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1101"></COL> i. (id est) 3 <SUP>a</SUP>  eo 3 <SUP>b</SUP> . 5. 6.</NOTE>  quod in Romana
urbe administraverat rectoris officium commisere,
et egregium virum tanta liberalitate et amicitia fovere,
ut nequaquam ulterius <NOTE N="324" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1101"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  5.</NOTE>  cuperet <NOTE N="325" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1101"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  3 <SUP>b</SUP> . ad p. remearet
5. 6.</NOTE>  ad patriam
remeare. Adhuc autem <NOTE N="326" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1101"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  5.</NOTE>  eo Romanum jus
regente, contigit quendam <NOTE N="327" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1101"></COL> reum q. n. e. (eptem 6 <SUP>b</SUP> .) ab ipso 6.</NOTE>  nomine Epten reum
 <COL N="1101B"></COL> ab ipso Arimaspe <NOTE N="328" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1101"></COL> armaspe 5. arismaspe 6 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  capite condempnari. Qui judicium
fugiens, hac et illac <NOTE N="329" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1101"></COL> hac
illacque 1. 1 <SUP>b</SUP> . hac illac 5 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  incertus vagabatur
et <NOTE N="330" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1101"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  5 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  profugus. Hic ergo <NOTE N="331" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1101"></COL> vero 3 <SUP>b</SUP>  5. 6. B2.</NOTE>  ubi <NOTE N="332" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1101"></COL> ubi audivit f. 1. 1 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  fama volante <NOTE N="333" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1101"></COL> volitante qual.
5.</NOTE> 
cognovit, qualibus honoribus Arimaspes <NOTE N="334" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1101"></COL> armaspes 1 <SUP>b</SUP> . 5.</NOTE>  in Treberis
floreret, invidit, et mortem sibi olim ab ipso <NOTE N="335" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1101"></COL> eo 6 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE> 
destinatam ulcisci desiderans, Treberim venit; ubi
se nemine cognoscente et ob hoc nihil <NOTE N="336" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1101"></COL> in se nichil 6 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  in se sinistri
suspicante, tandem post multas [insidias <NOTE N="337" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1101"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita 2. 3. 5. 6. post add.</HI>  C1.  <HI REND="ITALIC">et ita</HI>  C3.  <HI REND="ITALIC">seqq.
deest</HI>  1. 1 <SUP>b</SUP> . B. multa B2. 4.</NOTE> ]
Arimaspem inventum occidit. Qui sentiens hoc se <NOTE N="338" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1101"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  3 <SUP>b</SUP> . 5. h. u. m. se non 6 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE> 
vulnere mortem non posse effugere, in porta Martia
se rogavit sepeliri et hoc <NOTE N="339" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1101"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  5 <SUP>c</SUP> .</NOTE>  epitaphium <NOTE N="340" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1101"></COL> epitaphio 2.</NOTE>  ad gratiam
 <COL N="1102A"></COL> <NOTE N="341" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1101"></COL> ad
treberorum gratiam 6 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  Trebirorum, sepulcro suo super <NOTE N="342" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1101"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  5 <SUP>b</SUP>  B2. 6.</NOTE>  inscribi
 <NOTE N="343" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1101"></COL> i. fecit 3. 5. 6.—C1. 3.  <HI REND="ITALIC">add. rubram:</HI>  Epit. Arimasp.</NOTE> :

 <POEM COM="1102"><L><HI REND="ITALIC">Exul Arimaspes hac Martis</HI> <NOTE N="344" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1101"></COL> martis—multo gravius hoc ( <HI REND="ITALIC">infra c. 9.) desunt 1 <SUP>b</SUP> . folio amisso.</HI></NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">in arce quiesco</HI></L> <L INDENT=1><HI REND="ITALIC">Belgica</HI> <NOTE N="345" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1101"></COL> bellica B3. 4.</NOTE> ;  <HI REND="ITALIC">Roma mei non</HI> <NOTE N="346" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1101"></COL> in 2.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">mea digna</HI> <NOTE N="347" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1101"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  5 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">fuit.</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">Jure bono, meritorum nobilitate, triumphis</HI></L> <L INDENT=1><HI REND="ITALIC">Dii</HI> <NOTE N="348" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1101"></COL> Hii 3 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">tueantur, ei</HI> <NOTE N="349" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1101"></COL> tueantur eam 2.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">par nisi Roma nichil.</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">Vulneror, Epte reo, consul primusque senatus</HI> <NOTE N="350" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1101"></COL> senator B2. 3.</NOTE> .</L> <L INDENT=1><HI REND="ITALIC">Hic gaudete</HI> <NOTE N="351" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1101"></COL> gaudere 5.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">mei, sic meruisse mori.</HI></L></POEM></P> <P COM="1102">9 <NOTE N="352" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1101"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">c.</HI>  XI.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Leibn.</HI></NOTE> . Anno <NOTE N="(198)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="1102" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1102C"></COL> Quae sequuntur ad verbum plerumque ex
