Erat <NOTE N="628" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> Erat autem inter ipsos 5 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  inter eos et Labienum difficili transitu flumen
ripisque praeruptis. Hoc neque ipse <NOTE N="629" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> i. n. C3.</NOTE>  transire
in animo <NOTE N="630" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> in a.  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  1. 1 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  habebat, neque Trebiros transituros <NOTE N="631" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> transire 1. 1 <SUP>b</SUP> . 5.</NOTE> 
existimabat. Augebatur auxiliorum <NOTE N="632" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> c. a. B. C. Aux. s. c. t. augebatur 5. 6. agebatur 6 <SUP>c</SUP> .</NOTE>  cottidie spes
Treberis. Labienus loquitur in consilio <NOTE N="633" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> concilio 2. 6.</NOTE>  palam,
quoniam Germani appropinquare <NOTE N="634" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> appropinquarentur  <HI REND="ITALIC">e corr.</HI>  1.</NOTE>  dicantur <NOTE N="635" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> dicantur  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  1. 1 <SUP>b</SUP> . dicuntur 5 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> ,
sese <NOTE N="636" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> se B2.</NOTE>  suas exercitusque fortunas in dubium non <NOTE N="637" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  2.</NOTE> 
devocaturum, et postero <NOTE N="638" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> postera 5 <SUP>b</SUP> . B2.  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  postero 6 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  die prima luce castra
moturum. Celeriter haec ad Trebiros deferuntur, et
 <COL N="1109B"></COL> ex magno suorum equitatus numero nonnullos <NOTE N="639" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> nonnullis B2.</NOTE> 
Gallicis rebus favere natura cogebat. Labienus nocte
tribunis militum <NOTE N="640" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> milites 1. tribunos milites 1 <SUP>b</SUP> . millenis 2. 3 <SUP>b</SUP> . 4. 5. 6. m. premissisque 5 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  primisque ordinibus coactis,
quid sit <NOTE N="641" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> sui sit
B. C.</NOTE>  sui consilii proponit, et quo facilius det <NOTE N="642" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> de 5 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> 
hostibus timoris <NOTE N="643" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> t. sui 5 <SUP>c</SUP> .</NOTE>  suspitionem, majore <NOTE N="644" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> majori 6.</NOTE>  strepitu
et tumultu quam publicae rei <NOTE N="645" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> res 1. publica res fieri 1 <SUP>b</SUP> .—populi Romani  <HI REND="ITALIC">scribendum
erat.</HI></NOTE>  fert consuetudo,
castra moveri jubet. His <NOTE N="646" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> Is. 1. jussit his 1 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  rebus fugae <NOTE N="647" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> s. f. 5.</NOTE>  similem
profectionem efficit <NOTE N="648" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> effecit 1. 6 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE> . Haec quoque per exploratores
ante lucem ad Trebiros deferuntur. Vix agmen novissimum
extra munitiones <NOTE N="649" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> munitionem B. C.</NOTE>  processerat <NOTE N="650" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> processerant 1. 1 <SUP>b</SUP> .—cujus
g. 1 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE> , cum
Galli cohortati inter se, ne <NOTE N="651" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  B. 6.</NOTE>  speratam praedam ex
manibus dimitterent; longum esse, perterritis Romanis
 <NOTE N="652" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> hostibus 3 <SUP>b</SUP> . 5. 6.</NOTE> , Germanos expectare, neque suam pati
dignitatem, ut tantis copiis tam exiguam manum
praesertim fugientem atque <NOTE N="653" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> atque  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  5. 6. a. i.  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  B2. 4? C3. imp.  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  B6. C1
( <HI REND="ITALIC">ubi post</HI>  atque  <HI REND="ITALIC">deletum</HI> ). C6.</NOTE>  impeditam adoriri non
 <COL N="1109C"></COL> audeant. Flumen transire et in loco iniquo <NOTE N="654" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> loco in quo b. 1 <SUP>b</SUP> . 3 <SUP>b</SUP> . 5 <SUP>b</SUP> . <SUP>c</SUP> . locum in quo bellum 5 <SUP>a</SUP> . l. quo illi steterant 6.</NOTE>  bellum
committere non dubitant <NOTE N="655" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> dubitabant 1 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE> . Quod fore suspicatus
Labienus, ut omnes citra flumen eliceret, eadem
usus simulatione itineris, placide progrediebatur
 <NOTE N="656" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> egrediebatur 2. 3 <SUP>b</SUP> . 4? 5. 6. B. C. e. p. 6.</NOTE> . Tum <NOTE N="657" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> Tunc 5 <SUP>c</SUP> . 6.</NOTE>  premissis <NOTE N="658" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> remissis B. C.</NOTE>  paululum impedimentis
atque in tumulo quodam <NOTE N="659" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI> 
1. 1 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  collocatis, cohortatus
milites, simul signa ad Gallos converti aciemque
dirigi jubet. Paucis turmis <NOTE N="660" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> terminis 1 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  praesidio <NOTE N="661" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  2. 5. 6. B. C.</NOTE>  ad impedimenta
dimissis, reliquos equites ad latera disponit.
Romani celeriter clamore sublato, pila <NOTE N="662" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> palam 3 <SUP>b</SUP> . 5. 6.</NOTE>  in
 <COL N="1110A"></COL> Trebiros mittunt. Illi ubi praeter <NOTE N="663" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  1 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  spem quos fugere
credebant infestis signis ad se ire <NOTE N="664" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> adire 1 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  videre,
impetum modo ferre non potuerunt, ac primo concursu
in fugam conjecti <NOTE N="665" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> versi 1 <SUP>b</SUP> .
conversi 2.</NOTE> , proximas silvas petierunt.
Quos Labienus equitatu consectatus <NOTE N="666" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> consecutus 1 <SUP>b</SUP> . 5. 6. consequtus  <HI REND="ITALIC">superscr.</HI>  consectatus 3 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE> , magno
numero interfecto, compluribus captis, paucis
post diebus civitatem recepit. Nam Germani qui
auxilio venerant, percepta <NOTE N="667" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> per certa 1 <SUP>b</SUP> . audita 6.</NOTE>  Trebirorum fuga, sese
domum <NOTE N="668" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> d.
sese 5. 6.</NOTE>  contulerunt. Cum hiis Induciomari propinqui,
qui <NOTE N="669" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  B6.</NOTE>  defectionis <NOTE N="670" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> factionis 2.</NOTE>  auctores fuerant <NOTE N="671" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> extiterant 1. 1 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE> ,
comitati eos ex civitate <NOTE N="672" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> ex c.  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  1. 1 <SUP>b</SUP> . eos civitati 6.</NOTE>  excesserunt <NOTE N="673" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> excesserant
1. 1 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE> . Cingetorigi
 <NOTE N="674" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> cingetori 2.  <HI REND="ITALIC">hoc loco.</HI></NOTE> , quem ab initio permansisse in <NOTE N="675" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> d. in o. 1. 1 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  officio demonstravimus,
principatus atque imperium <NOTE N="676" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> p. imperiumque 1. 1 <SUP>b</SUP> . i. contraditum 1 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  est
traditum. Caesar <NOTE N="677" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">c.</HI>  XVI.  <HI REND="ITALIC">inc. Leibn.</HI></NOTE>  vero postquam ex Menapiis in
Trebiros <NOTE N="678" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> treveris. B6.</NOTE>  venit, duabus de <NOTE N="679" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> ex B. C.</NOTE>  causis Renum transire
 <COL N="1110B"></COL> voluit. Quarum <NOTE N="680" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> quorum 1. C1. 3.</NOTE>  erat <NOTE N="681" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> a. e. 5. 6.</NOTE>  altera, quod contra se
auxilia Treberis miserant <NOTE N="682" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> m. treb.
1. 1 <SUP>b</SUP> . miserint 2.</NOTE> , altera ne Ambiorix
receptum <NOTE N="683" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> respectum 2.</NOTE>  ad eos haberet. Firmo in Treberis <NOTE N="684" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> trebiris  <HI REND="ITALIC">etiam hoc loco</HI>  2.</NOTE> 
praesidio ad pontem relicto, ne quis ab <NOTE N="685" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> ab ipso 1 <SUP>b</SUP> . q. s. m. ab h. 6.</NOTE>  his subito
motus oriretur, cum reliquis copiis contra Suevos,
qui auxilia Treberis miserant, Renum transivit.</P> <P COM="1110">11.  <CITN>(CAES. VI, 11.)</CITN>  Non alienum videtur esse, de
moribus Trebirorum <NOTE N="(201)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> Treveros hoc loco non Caesar sed scriptor Treverensis nominat.</NOTE>  vel Gallorum proponere,
quibus videlicet moribus ex parte foedus est laesum,
quod cum Romanis habuerant <NOTE N="686" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> habuerat
3 <SUP>b</SUP> . 5.</NOTE> . In Treberis <NOTE N="687" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> treberi 1. 1 <SUP>b</SUP> . 3 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(201)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> Treveros hoc loco non Caesar sed scriptor Treverensis nominat.</NOTE> 
non solum in omnibus pagis et partibus, sed <NOTE N="688" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  3 <SUP>b</SUP> . 5. B. C.</NOTE>  pene
etiam <NOTE N="689" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  6. et 3 <SUP>b</SUP> . 5.</NOTE>  in singulis domibus <NOTE N="690" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  2.</NOTE>  factiones, eorumque
 <NOTE N="691" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita codices
quos vidi omnes fere;</HI>  earumque 3 <SUP>b</SUP> . 5. 6.</NOTE>  factionum principes fuerunt, qui summam <NOTE N="692" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> summa auctoritate 5 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> 
auctoritatem eorum judicio habebant. Quorum ad
arbitrium judiciumque <NOTE N="693" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> judicium summaque 5.</NOTE>  summa omnium rerum
 <COL N="1110C"></COL> consiliorumque <NOTE N="694" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> judiciorumque
6.</NOTE>  rediebat <NOTE N="695" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> rediebat  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  redibat 1. rediebant  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  redibat 5 <SUP>a</SUP> . Cl. redibat 5 <SUP>c</SUP> . 6. C3.</NOTE> , idque ejus rei <NOTE N="696" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  2. 3 <SUP>b</SUP> .
5. 6. B. C.</NOTE> 
causa antiquitus institutum <NOTE N="697" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> i. est B. C.</NOTE> , ne quis <NOTE N="698" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> quid 1. 1 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  ex plebe
contra potentiorem auxilii <NOTE N="699" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> auxilio 2.—egerat 1 <SUP>b</SUP> .—Suo 2.</NOTE>  egeret. Suos enim
quisque opprimi et circumveniri <NOTE N="700" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> circumvenire B2.</NOTE>  non patitur.
Neque enim aliter <NOTE N="701" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  2. 3 <SUP>b</SUP> . 5. 6.</NOTE>  si faciant, ullam <NOTE N="702" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> et illam 5 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  inter suos
habent <NOTE N="703" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> haberent 5 <SUP>a</SUP> . <SUP>b</SUP> . 6. habere 5 <SUP>c</SUP> .</NOTE>  auctoritatem. Haec eadem ratio <NOTE N="704" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> ratione in 1 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  est in
summa totius Galliae  <CITN>(cf. V, 3)</CITN> . Namque haec civitas
ideo detrimentum sustinuit, quia alterius factionis
erat Induciomarus, alterius Cingetorix <NOTE N="705" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> cingetor 3 <SUP>b</SUP> .
5. 6.  <HI REND="ITALIC">ut aliis locis.</HI></NOTE> . In <NOTE N="706" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">c.</HI>  XVII.  <HI REND="ITALIC">inc. Leibn.</HI></NOTE> 
ea <NOTE N="707" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1109"></COL> Interea 6.</NOTE>  sicut et in omni Gallia eorum hominum qui in
 <COL N="1111A"></COL> aliquo numero <NOTE N="708" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1111"></COL> munere 2.</NOTE>  et honore <NOTE N="709" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1111"></COL> et h.  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  1. 1 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  censentur genera
erant duo. Nam plebes <NOTE N="710" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1111"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita</HI>  1. 1 <SUP>b</SUP> . 2. 3 <SUP>b</SUP> . 5 <SUP>a</SUP> . <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  pene servorum habebatur
loco, quae <NOTE N="711" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1111"></COL> quae—consilio  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  5.</NOTE>  per se nichil audebat <NOTE N="712" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1111"></COL> audiebat 6.</NOTE> , nulli adhibebatur
consilio. Plerique cum aere alieno aut magnitudine
tributorum aut injuria potentiorum premebantur,
in servitutem se dicabant nobilibus. In hos
omnia jura quae domini in servos. Sed de <NOTE N="713" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1111"></COL> in 5 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  hiis
duobus generibus alterum erat driuidum <NOTE N="714" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1111"></COL> druudum 1 <SUP>b</SUP> . drudum 6.  <HI REND="ITALIC">semper, hoc loco etiam</HI>  3 <SUP>b</SUP> . drudum  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  druidum 5 <SUP>a</SUP> . drudum 5 <SUP>b</SUP> . drundum 5 <SUP>c</SUP> .
 <HI REND="ITALIC">et ita postea.</HI>  driuitum B2.</NOTE>  [id est
philosophorum  <HI REND="ITALIC">add.,</HI>  B. C.], alterum <NOTE N="715" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1111"></COL> a. erat 6.</NOTE>  equitum.
Illi rebus divinis <NOTE N="716" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1111"></COL> r. de rebus  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  d. r. C1. d. r. 6. C3.</NOTE>  intererant, sacrificia publica
ac <NOTE N="717" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1111"></COL> et 5 <SUP>a</SUP> . <SUP>c</SUP> .</NOTE>  privata procurabant, religionem <NOTE N="718" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1111"></COL> religione 1.</NOTE>  interpretabantur.
Ad hos magnus adolescentium numerus
disciplinae causa concurrebat, magnoque hii erant <NOTE N="719" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1111"></COL> a. eos erant h. 2. 6.</NOTE> 
apud eos honore. Nam <NOTE N="720" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1111"></COL> Namque C6.</NOTE>  fere de omnibus controversiis
publicis privatisque constituebant, et si quod
 <COL N="1111B"></COL> facinus admissum, si caedes facta, si de hereditate,
de <NOTE N="721" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1111"></COL> si. d. 6.</NOTE>  finibus controversia erat, idem decernebant
 <NOTE N="722" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1111"></COL> decernabant 6 <SUP>a</SUP> . determinabant 5 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE> , praemia poenasque constituebant. Si qui <NOTE N="723" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1111"></COL> quid 2.</NOTE> 
aut privati <NOTE N="724" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1111"></COL> privatim
B2. C.</NOTE>  aut populus eorum decreto non obediebat
 <NOTE N="725" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="1111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="1111"></COL> obediebant i. aditum 3 <SUP>b</SUP> . 5. 6.</NOTE> , interdicebant. Haec poena apud eos gravissima
